   567	  so the failure probability exp(−e^{Ω(E)}) per target beats the union bound over e^{O(Q)} targets whenever
   568	  2s > φ/3 (`barrier.ad_heuristic_ok`). Example: δ = 1/2, b₁ = 1 (τ_F = 1/2), λ = 1/2, b = 4, κ_F = 4, m₀ = 2 (design
   569	  (a‴) with M ≈ H ≈ N^{1/(d+1)}, so log M ≈ Q/δ), s = 3/4 satisfies the heuristic and gives c_NR ≈ 26.7
   570	  (unoptimised; `barrier.nr_constant`).
   571	- **AD is exactly what §§3–5 say we cannot prove.** It is a pointwise-in-the-field statement about smooth values of
   572	  one binary form of degree d ≍ D′ on special-q lattices at L-scale. Averaging over 𝔉 cannot certify it by moments
   573	  (§6: Θ(1) relative variance across fields; overdetermination for joint statements).
   574	- AD for *every* target is stronger than needed (only targets that occur matter), but any weaker endogenous version
   575	  runs into Prop SI(i).
